        "itemId": 17592186676167,
        "kind": "question",
        "knowledgePoint": null,
        "markdown": "If the equation ${log}_{2}\u2061(128)=7$ is equivalent to ${b}^{7}=128,$  then $b=${{field-1}}.",
        "mathAcademyId": "q-252538",
        "requiresCalculator": null,
        "solution": "The logarithm of $a$ with base $b$ is defined as follows:\n\n${log}_{b}\u2061a=x$ is equivalent to $a={b}^{x}$\n\nIf we compare ${log}_{2}\u2061(128)=7$ with ${log}_{b}\u2061a=x,$ we get $a=128,$ $b=2,$ and $x=7.$\n\nTherefore, the given equation is equivalent to ${2}^{7}=128.$ Consequently,  $b=2.$",
        "status": "correct",
        "stepId": "17592186676083",
        "title": "Practice"
      },
      "total": 9
    },
