        "itemId": 17592186676173,
        "kind": "question",
        "knowledgePoint": null,
        "markdown": "Find $Ax$ if\n$$\n\\displaystyle A = \\begin{bmatrix}2a & 3c \\\\ 2b & 2d\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\nand\n$$\n\\displaystyle x = \\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$",
        "mathAcademyId": null,
        "requiresCalculator": null,
        "solution": "We multiply each row in the matrix by the column vector using the dot product:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Ax & =\\begin{bmatrix}2a & 3c \\\\ 2b & 2d\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ & =\\begin{bmatrix}2a\\cdot 3+3c\\cdot 2 \\\\ 2b\\cdot 3+2d\\cdot 2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ & =\\begin{bmatrix}6a+6c \\\\ 6b+4d\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
        "status": "correct",
        "stepId": "17592186676086",
        "title": "Practice"
      },
