        "itemId": 17592186676174,
        "kind": "question",
        "knowledgePoint": null,
        "markdown": "$\\ln\\left(\\frac{8}{e^{5}}\\right)=$",
        "mathAcademyId": null,
        "requiresCalculator": null,
        "solution": "First, let's recall the quotient rule for natural logarithms:\n\n$$\n\\ln(a)-\\ln(b)=\\ln\\left(\\frac{a}{b}\\right)\n$$\n\nUsing the quotient rule for natural logarithms, the given expression can be rewritten as:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\ln\\left(\\frac{8}{e^{5}}\\right) &= \\ln(8)-\\ln(e^{5}) \\\\ &= \\ln(8)-5\\end{aligned}\n$$",
        "status": "correct",
        "stepId": "17592186676087",
        "title": "Practice"
