        "itemId": 17592186676175,
        "kind": "question",
        "knowledgePoint": null,
        "markdown": "Simplify $\\frac{{x}^{7}}{{x}^{12}}.$",
        "mathAcademyId": "q-72657",
        "requiresCalculator": null,
        "solution": "We subtract the exponents, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{x}^{7}}{{x}^{12}} & = \\\\ {x}^{(7-12)} & = \\\\ {x}^{-5} & \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we convert the negative exponent to a positive exponent by taking the reciprocal:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{-5} & =\\frac{1}{{x}^{5}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{7}}{{x}^{12}}=\\frac{1}{{x}^{5}}.\n$$",
        "status": "correct",
        "stepId": "17592186676088",
        "title": "Practice"
      },
      "total": 9
