        "itemId": 17592186676176,
        "kind": "question",
        "knowledgePoint": null,
        "markdown": "Express $4\\operatorname{log}\u20612+4\\operatorname{log}\u20614+4\\operatorname{log}\u20618$ as a single logarithm.",
        "mathAcademyId": "q-108100",
        "requiresCalculator": null,
        "solution": "First, let's recall the product rule for logarithms:\n\n$$\n{log}_{n}\u2061a+{log}_{n}\u2061b={log}_{n}\u2061(ab)\n$$\n\nIf we factor the given expression and use the product rule for logarithms, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4\\operatorname{log}\u20612+4\\operatorname{log}\u20614+4\\operatorname{log}\u20618 & =4(\\operatorname{log}\u20612+4\\operatorname{log}\u20614+\\operatorname{log}\u20618) \\\\  & =4\\operatorname{log}\u2061(2\\cdot 4\\cdot 8) \\\\  & =4\\operatorname{log}\u206164.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n4\\operatorname{log}\u20612+4\\operatorname{log}\u20614+4\\operatorname{log}\u20618=4\\operatorname{log}\u206164.\n$$",
        "status": "correct",
        "stepId": "17592186676089",
        "title": "Practice"
      },
