        "itemId": 17592186676177,
        "kind": "question",
        "knowledgePoint": null,
        "markdown": "Assume all variables are positive. Which of the following is equivalent to $\\left(5t^{-2}u^{-1}\\right)^{3}$?",
        "mathAcademyId": null,
        "requiresCalculator": null,
        "solution": "We apply the power of product rule and then simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\left(5t^{-2}u^{-1}\\right)^{3} &= 5^{3}\\cdot \\left(t^{-2}\\right)^{3}\\cdot \\left(u^{-1}\\right)^{3} \\\\ &= 5^{3}\\cdot t^{(-2)\\cdot (3)}\\cdot u^{(-1)\\cdot (3)} \\\\ &= 125t^{-6}u^{-3} \\\\ &= \\frac{125}{t^{6}u^{3}}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
        "status": "correct",
        "stepId": "17592186676090",
        "title": "Practice"
